{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15779","formula":"C₇H₈","hill":"C7H8","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":8.0},"names":{"en":"Toluene","ru":"Толуол","uk":"Толуен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Toluene (), also known as toluol (), is a substituted aromatic hydrocarbon with the chemical formula C6H5CH3, often abbreviated as PhCH3, where Ph stands for the phenyl group. Toluene is a colorless, water-insoluble liquid with a sweet smell, and is partially responsible for the aroma of gasoline and paint fumes. It is a mono-substituted benzene derivative, consisting of a methyl group (CH3) attached to a phenyl group by a single bond.","ru":"Толуо́л (от исп. Tolu, толуанский бальзам; фенилметан, метилбензол, сокращённое химическое обозначение — PhMe) — ароматический углеводород с химической формулой C6H5CH3. Бесцветная жидкость с характерным запахом, относится к аренам.","uk":"Толуен або толуол — гомолог бензену."},"fame":67,"pubchemCid":1140,"mass":92.14,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC=CC=C1","inchikey":"YXFVVABEGXRONW-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"toluene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1140","atoms":15,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.983,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.285,"y":1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.285,"y":-1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.474,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.11,"y":1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.11,"y":-1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.807,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.817,"y":2.156,"z":-0.002,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.817,"y":-2.156,"z":-0.002,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.869,"y":-0.88,"z":0.518,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.869,"y":0.881,"z":0.517,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.849,"y":0.0,"z":-1.028,"el":"H"},{"x":1.653,"y":2.148,"z":-0.001,"el":"H"},{"x":1.653,"y":-2.148,"z":-0.001,"el":"H"},{"x":2.893,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2],[0,2,1],[0,3,1],[1,4,1]